# Nov 16 2026 (KPC owner): LINE ENDINGS. Several hashes in this club are worked out from the BYTES of files in this
# repository, not from their meaning:
#   * the answer-key rules hash (.github/scripts/kpc_key_freeze.py rules_hash) over the RULE FILES, which the 2-fer key
#     gate compares against every key build;
#   * the per-area 2-fer input hash (KPC-Data .github/scripts/kpc_fers_chain_plan.py) over data/<key>/<AREA>.json and the
#     outline files.
# Git for Windows writes CRLF on checkout by default. A Windows checkout of the very same commit then held different bytes
# and worked out different hashes than the club's own Linux builds: the PC 2-fer runner's key gate called every green key
# stale (us-key 3759b3c8b122 instead of d4ebfafce438) and refused all 65 areas. These lines keep every checkout, on every
# machine, byte for byte what this repository holds: LF.
# rules_hash also levels line endings itself, so this file is the second lock, not the only one.
# ADD A LINE HERE for a new rule file that is not already covered by the patterns.

# every JSON file: the answer keys, the rule tables, the scope files, the area tables, canada-bounds
*.json text eol=lf
*.geojson text eol=lf

# the rule scripts named in RULE_FILES

.github/scripts/kpc_ca_fill_bounds.py text eol=lf
.github/scripts/kpc_ca_hardlook.py text eol=lf
